{"name":"Coffee Grounds","hex":"#302010","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coffee grounds","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sediment that remains after ground coffee beans have been extracted with hot water.","Synonym of coffee ground vomitus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coffee_grounds"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coffee preparation","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee preparation is the process of making liquid coffee using coffee beans. While the particular steps vary with the type of coffee and with the raw materials, the process includes four basic steps: raw coffee beans must be roasted, the roasted coffee beans must then be ground, and the ground coffee must then be mixed with hot or cold water for a specific time (brewed), the liquid coffee extraction must be separated from the used grounds, and finally, if desired, the extracted coffee is combined with other elements of the desired beverage, such as sweeteners, dairy products, dairy alternatives, or toppings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/TEDxAMS2011_044.JPG/330px-TEDxAMS2011_044.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_preparation"},{"title":"Coffee","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a beverage brewed from roasted, ground coffee beans. Dark-colored and bitter, coffee has a stimulating effect on humans due to its caffeine content; however decaffeinated coffee is also commercially available. There are also various coffee substitutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg/330px-Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee"},{"title":"Coffee (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a brownish color that is a representation of a roasted coffee bean. Different types of coffee beans have different colors when roasted—the color coffee represents an average."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Interieur%2C_cycloon-machine_-_Hilversum_-_20346981_-_RCE.jpg/500px-Interieur%2C_cycloon-machine_-_Hilversum_-_20346981_-_RCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Interieur%2C_cycloon-machine_-_Hilversum_-_20346981_-_RCE.jpg/1280px-Interieur%2C_cycloon-machine_-_Hilversum_-_20346981_-_RCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Interieur%2C_cycloon-machine_-_Hilversum_-_20346981_-_RCE.jpg/500px-Interieur%2C_cycloon-machine_-_Hilversum_-_20346981_-_RCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dutch coffee-roasting machine, c. 1920","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInterieur%2C_cycloon-machine_-_Hilversum_-_20346981_-_RCE.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Mlynek.jpg/330px-Mlynek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Mlynek.jpg/330px-Mlynek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An old-fashioned manual burr-mill coffee grinder","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMlynek.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Coffee-IMG_7048-white.jpg/500px-Coffee-IMG_7048-white.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Coffee-IMG_7048-white.jpg/1280px-Coffe